{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":208007,"duration_api_ms":202537,"num_turns":40,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"b2458a99-6aed-4b50-a929-f89096fbed31","total_cost_usd":1.5860625,"usage":{"input_tokens":31,"cache_creation_input_tokens":78696,"cache_read_input_tokens":1863415,"output_tokens":6494,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":78696,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":31,"outputTokens":6494,"cacheReadInputTokens":1863415,"cacheCreationInputTokens":78696,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.5860625,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Reviewed all changes for tanksim-6e5.7.3 (apply_fixes cycle 2 round 1). The diff touches 4 files: `docs/validation_scenarios.md` (doc updates for VS-03 and VS-07), `e2e_validation_suite.rs` (substantial VS-03 and VS-07 scenario hardening), `e2e_carbonate_probes.rs` (aligned probe_3 with VS-03 changes), and `presets.rs` (removed `temp_condition_min_factor` from strictly-positive validation list + added test for zero). All 8 validation scenarios pass (8/8), clippy is clean, carbonate probes pass. The changes are internally consistent: envelope bounds tightened from [0.1, 2.0] to [0.2, 1.0] for pH swing, VS-07 reworked with longer horizon (120d), zero-nitrate refill water, identical plant loads, and a new directional NO₃ gap assertion. The presets.rs change correctly allows zero for `temp_condition_min_factor` while keeping it in the non-negative validation list. One moderate concern and one minor concern identified.","amendments":[{"body":"In VS-07 (nitrate removal), the bare-bottom arm sets `denitrification_vmax_mg_n_per_l_per_hour = 0.2` and `denitrification_pore_water_mixing_factor = 1.0` but has no substrate (`substrate_layers.clear()`). The comment says the substrate removal eliminates the denitrification pathway, so these process params are presumably inert without substrate. However, explicitly zeroing these params on the bare arm (or adding a comment explaining that substrate absence makes them no-ops) would make the test's intent clearer and guard against future model changes that might introduce a water-column denitrification pathway where these params would suddenly matter.","rationale":"If a future model revision adds a non-substrate denitrification pathway (e.g., water-column heterotrophic denitrification), the bare arm would unexpectedly activate denitrification with these non-zero params, silently invalidating the scenario's control. Setting them to 0.0 on the bare arm is the defensive choice."},{"body":"The validation_scenarios.md report template (lines 508-511) still references `maturity=X.XX` in the VS-01 cycling checkpoints, but the scenario's code and envelope bounds no longer validate the biofilter maturity index (the doc note at line 69-72 explicitly says cycling completion is validated by nitrification output, not maturity index). The template should drop the maturity field from the checkpoint lines or add a note that it is reported for observability only, to avoid confusion when the calibration workflow (G4) auto-populates it.","rationale":"Minor doc-test inconsistency. The template implies maturity is a validated metric when it is explicitly excluded from the envelope checks. A developer auto-populating this template might expect maturity to have pass/fail criteria."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"a7d87df8-701a-4b5c-bd96-257db9557e79"}
